@startuml
title Stage 0.5 - ChannelRuntimeMeta TTL Window (Write in A, Read in C)

hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

participant "DummyDetectionNode (A)" as A
participant "OutputNode (C)" as C
participant "ChannelRuntimeMetaStore\n(mutex; read=find-only)" as Store
participant "ChannelRuntimeMeta" as Meta
participant "Logger" as Logger

== A updates meta (write can create) ==
A -> Store : write(channel_id, callback)
activate Store
Store -> Meta : get_or_create(channel_id)\n(WRITE path)
Store -> Meta : last_seen_vehicle = now_mono_ns
deactivate Store

== C reads meta (read must not create) ==
C -> Store : read(channel_id, callback)
activate Store
alt meta exists
  Store -> Meta : find(channel_id)\n(READ path)
  Store --> C : callback(const Meta&)\nC computes is_vehicle_present(now)
  C -> Logger : info(sample)\nvehicle_present=true/false
else meta missing
  Store --> C : return (no callback)
  C -> Logger : (optional) debug sample\nmeta_missing=true
end
deactivate Store

note right of Store
Design decision (4.1):
- read() must never create.
- write() may create.
end note

@enduml
